1
00:06:06,666 --> 00:06:12,666
Life, liberty, and the pursuit of vengeance.

2
00:12:13,333 --> 00:12:19,333
Django Unchained is a drama, western film directed by Quentin Tarantino.

3
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:26,000
With the help of a German bounty hunter, a freed slave sets out to
rescue his wife from a brutal Mississippi plantation owner.

4
00:24:26,666 --> 00:24:32,666
Django Freeman, played by Jamie Foxx.

5
00:30:33,333 --> 00:30:39,333
Dr. King Schultz, played by Christoph Waltz.

6
00:36:40,000 --> 00:36:46,000
Calvin J. Candie, played by Leonardo DiCaprio.

7
00:42:46,666 --> 00:42:52,666
Broomhilda von Shaft, played by Kerry Washington.

8
00:48:53,333 --> 00:48:59,333
Stephen, played by Samuel L. Jackson.

9
00:55:00,000 --> 00:55:06,000
Billy Crash, played by Walton Goggins.

10
01:01:06,666 --> 01:01:12,666
Django Unchained ( JANG-goh) is a 2012 American revisionist
Western film written and directed by Quentin Tarantino.

11
01:07:13,333 --> 01:07:19,333
Produced by Tarantino's A Band Apart and Columbia Pictures, it stars Jamie Foxx,
Christoph Waltz, Leonardo DiCaprio, Kerry Washington, and Samuel L.

12
01:13:20,000 --> 01:13:26,000
Jackson with Walton Goggins, Dennis Christopher, James Remar,
Michael Parks, and Don Johnson in supporting roles.

13
01:19:26,666 --> 01:19:32,666
The film, set in the Antebellum South and Old West follows the story of an enslaved man who trains
under a German bounty hunter with the ultimate goal of reuniting with his wife.

14
01:25:33,333 --> 01:25:39,333
It is a highly stylized, revisionist tribute to spaghetti Westerns, with its title
referring particularly to the 1966 Italian film Django by Sergio Corbucci.

15
01:31:40,000 --> 01:31:46,000
Development of Django Unchained began in 2007, when
Tarantino was writing a book on Corbucci.

16
01:37:46,666 --> 01:37:52,666
By April 2011, Tarantino sent his final draft of the
script to The Weinstein Company (TWC).

17
01:43:53,333 --> 01:43:59,333
Casting began in the summer of 2011, with Michael K.

18
01:50:00,000 --> 01:50:06,000
Williams and Will Smith being considered for the role of
the title character before Foxx was cast.

19
01:56:06,666 --> 01:56:12,666
Principal photography took place from November 2011 to March
2012 in California, Wyoming, and Louisiana.

20
02:02:13,333 --> 02:02:19,333
Django Unchained premiered at the Ziegfeld Theatre in New York City on December 11, 2012, and was theatrically released by The Weinstein
Company on December 25, in the United States, with Sony Pictures Releasing International handling international distribution.

21
02:08:20,000 --> 02:08:26,000
It was a commercial success, grossing $449.8 million worldwide against a $100 million budget, becoming
Tarantino's highest-grossing film to date, as well as the highest-grossing Western film of all time.

22
02:14:26,666 --> 02:14:32,666
The film received widespread acclaim from critics, who praised the performances especially those of Waltz, DiCaprio and Jackson and Tarantino's
direction and screenplay, though the film's extensive graphic violence and frequent use of racial slurs were source of controversy.

23
02:20:33,333 --> 02:20:39,333
It was named one of the top ten films of the year by the American Film Institute and by the National Board of Review, and received numerous accolades, gathering five
nominations at the 85th Academy Awards—including for Best Picture—winning for Best Supporting Actor (Waltz) and Best Original Screenplay (Tarantino).

24
02:26:40,000 --> 02:26:46,000
It also received five nominations with two wins at both the 70th Golden
Globe Awards and the 66th British Academy Film Awards.

25
02:32:46,666 --> 02:32:52,666
The film explores themes of rescue, friendship, bounty hunter, texas, slavery.

26
02:38:53,333 --> 02:38:59,333
The tone is dark and emotional.
